gaps.proposedFix:
Declare the exception set on the tlvList itself:
{ "tlvList": { "t":"u8", "l":"u8", "bare":["0x00","0xff"], "until":{"type":"0xff"} } }
A type octet listed in `bare` consumes exactly one byte, has no length and no value, and is not emitted as an item (PAD) or ends the walk (END). Same list is honoured on encode.

Add an optional `via` to any decode field, applied after the read and inverted on encode:
{ "u32be":null, "as":"yiaddr", "via":"ipv4" }
{ "value":null, "repeat":6, "as":"chaddr", "via":"mac" }
Require every converter usable in `via` to declare an inverse (ipv4/mac/ascii/hex/bcd all have one; md5 does not), which keeps the round-trip property checkable at validate time.

Make the frame and the overflow rule explicit:
{ "pad": { "to":300, "of":"message", "with":"00", "side":"right", "onOverflow":"ignore" } }
`of` ∈ message | layer | group:<name>; `onOverflow` ∈ ignore | error | truncate. Default `error`, so silence is never the answer.
